atoryPrepaymentsOnProceedsFromNonPermittedAssetSalesMember_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_SuperSeniorTermLoanMaturingJuly282028Member_vuyfE6MJDku4QXv1iCrkmA" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xbp:DebtInstrumentMandatoryPrepaymentThresholdNonpermittedAssetSalesTrigger" scale="6" id="Narr_xqeF78fjNkW5O4v5zZ5vAQ">0.5</ix:nonFraction> million in any fiscal year subject to reinvestment rights, (c) <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_ccSbwxZ2eE-Iz8EXGy6S7Q" contextRef="Duration_7_29_2025_To_7_29_2025_srt_StatementScenarioAxis_xbp_MandatoryPrepaymentsOnProceedsFromIssuancesMember_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_SuperSeniorTermLoanMaturingJuly282028Member_W---gVOwMk6CgFqCQCGSmA" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xbp:DebtInstrumentMandatoryPrepaymentPercentage" scale="-2" id="Narr_lOE4FkvKCk6-t2v2VhtgpA">100</ix:nonFraction>%<span style="white-space:pre-wrap;"> of net cash proceeds from the issuance of indebtedness or equity securities (other than permitted issuances), and (d) certain extraordinary receipts, such as insurance recoveries and condemnation awards, subject to reinvestment rights. Upon the occurrence of an event of default such as payment defaults, covenant breaches, bankruptcy or insolvency, cross-defaults to other significant indebtedness, and judgment defaults, the obligations under the Super Senior Term Loan may be accelerated and become immediately due and payable. On May 7, 2026, the Company entered into an amendment to the Super Senior Term Loan pursuant to which  the definition of "Permitted Securitization Financing" was amended to permit ongoing sales of designated receivables under the Amended BR Exar AR Facility (defined below), subject to a cap of </span>$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_bmzRMS-W4keOx5FozpRA5w" contextRef="As_Of_5_7_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_SuperSeniorTermLoanMaturingJuly282028Member_Z9PmIOztnUueAXRKDHyd9Q" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xbp:MaximumPermittedSalesOfDesignatedReceivables" scale="6" id="Narr_R0qbJalp0UqBWg0AuYEe4A">10.0</ix:nonFraction> million in the aggregate amount of Permitted Securitization Financings incurred and outstanding.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The obligations under the Super Senior Term Loan are guaranteed on a joint and several basis by substantially all of the Super Senior Term Loan Borrowers&#8217; subsidiaries and are secured by liens on the collateral of the Super Senior Term Loan Borrowers and the guarantors, subject to permitted liens and the terms of the ABL Intercreditor Agreement (as described below) and that certain Super Senior Intercreditor Agreement. The Super Senior Term Loan contains customary affirmative and negative covenants, including limitations on additional indebtedness, the granting of liens, asset sales, restricted payments, affiliate transactions, and changes in business. It also includes a financial covenant requiring the Issuer to maintain the ratio of (a) Indebtedness to (b) Covenant Consolidated EBITDA of no greater than <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_ccSbwxZ2eE-Iz8EXGy6S7Q" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_srt_RangeAxis_srt_MaximumMember_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_SuperSeniorTermLoanMaturingJuly282028Member_6XVXoRlJzkC2vZNdZgcsxw" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xbp:DebtInstrumentCovenantIndebtednessToConsolidatedEbitda" scale="0" id="Narr_jW_L-Jdh_Uyqho1md_5Iyw">1.00</ix:nonFraction> to 1.00 based on the trailing 12 months ended as of the last day of the most recently ended fiscal quarter. The Super Senior Term Loan Borrowers are also required to maintain liquidity of at least $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_bmzRMS-W4keOx5FozpRA5w" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_SuperSeniorTermLoanMaturingJuly282028Member_43zj87OYeU2HEKEV-rGqMQ" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xbp:DebtInstrumentCovenantMinimumLiquidityRequirement" scale="6" id="Narr_-sBJvwk1Q0SPBPQWPvsz5Q">2.0</ix:nonFraction> million. The Super Senior Term Loan Borrowers were in compliance with such financial covenants as of June 30, 2026.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">On August 14, 2026, the Super Senior Term Loan Borrowers, the agents and the required lenders entered into a limited waiver of the Specified Events of Default described below under &#8220;ABL Facility&#8221;, the effectiveness of which was subject to specified conditions and which requires the Company to satisfy specified post-closing obligations. See Note 15, <i style="font-style:italic;">Subsequent Events</i>.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Second Lien Note</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">On February 27, 2023, BPA, through its subsidiary Exela Receivables 3, LLC, and BRF Finance Co., LLC entered into a Secured Promissory Note pursuant to which BPA borrowed $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_bmzRMS-W4keOx5FozpRA5w" contextRef="Duration_2_27_2023_To_2_27_2023_dei_LegalEntityAxis_xbp_ExelaTechnologiesBpaLlcMember_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_SecondLienSecuredTermLoanMember_G-ZBz22KA0K1mTsPD8yY9A" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ProceedsFromIssuanceOfLongTermDebt" scale="6" id="Narr_UVwrqmfKY0G3fowrJf0jJg">31.5</ix:nonFraction> million from BRF Finance Co., LLC secured by a second lien pledge of Exela Receivables 3, LLC, a subsidiary of BPA (as amended, the &#8220;Second Lien Note&#8221;). The Second Lien Note was originally scheduled to mature on June 17, 2025 and bears interest at a per annum rate of one-month Term <span style="-sec-ix-hidden:Hidden_ihO91W8-BkCU3iujPq-HuQ;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">SOFR</span></span> plus <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_ccSbwxZ2eE-Iz8EXGy6S7Q" contextRef="Duration_2_27_2023_To_2_27_2023_dei_LegalEntityAxis_xbp_ExelaTechnologiesBpaLlcMember_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_SecondLienSecuredTermLoanMember_G-ZBz22KA0K1mTsPD8yY9A" decimals="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentBasisSpreadOnVariableRate1" scale="-2" id="Narr_8lhmIrq88U61IX12KrRdKA">7.5</ix:nonFraction>%. On July 29, 2025, BPA entered into an Amended and Restated Second Lien Credit Agreement with BRF Finance Co., LLC. The amendment was executed in connection with BPA&#8217;s emergence from the Chapter 11 Cases to align the terms of the Second Lien Note with the Company&#8217;s new capital structure and intercreditor arrangements. The Second Lien Note matures on September 30, 2026.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt;">The obligations under the Second Lien Note are fully and unconditionally guaranteed by certain subsidiaries of BPA and are secured by liens on BPA&#8217;s and certain guarantors&#8217; assets, including accounts receivable, inventory, cash and deposit accounts, equipment, real property, equity interests in subsidiaries, intercompany obligations, general intangibles, and other related assets. Pursuant to the ABL Intercreditor Agreement, BRF Finance Co., LLC&#8217;s liens are subordinated to the liens securing the Company&#8217;s senior debt facilities; specifically, the ABL Facility with respect to receivables, inventory, cash, and related assets, and the Super Senior Term Loan and July 2030 Notes with respect to </p></ix:continuation></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">26</p></div></div>
<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:79.3%;border:0;margin:30pt 10.35% 30pt 10.35%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:10.35%;padding-right:10.35%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:21.6pt;min-height:41.75pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;margin:0pt 0pt 30pt 0pt;"><a href="#TOC"><span style="font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Table of Contents</span></a></p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><ix:continuation id="Tb_dxRbl05eoEqfraXHXS3sTg_cont3" continuedAt="Tb_dxRbl05eoEqfraXHXS3sTg_cont4"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">fixed assets, equity interests, and other non-ABL assets. As a result, the obligations under the Second Lien Note are effectively second-priority liens behind the senior secured debt. The Second Lien Note includes a financial covenant requiring the borrowers to maintain a minimum fixed charge coverage ratio, calculated on a trailing twelve-month basis. The minimum required ratio varies depending on the period: for the defined periods tested quarterly through December 31, 2025, and monthly from January 1, 2026 through June 30, 2026, the fixed charge coverage ratio must be not less than <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_ccSbwxZ2eE-Iz8EXGy6S7Q" contextRef="As_Of_7_29_2025_srt_StatementScenarioAxis_xbp_DefinedPeriodTestedQuarterlyThroughDecember312025AndMonthlyFromJanuary12026ThroughJune302026Member_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_SecondLienSecuredTermLoanMember_v458CpLiRk6rV2kBvibxJw" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xbp:DebtInstrumentCovenantMinimumFixedChargeCoverageRatio" scale="0" id="Narr_-nvNlFdKKUGwtWjxOYwe4g">0.85</ix:nonFraction> to 1.00. Thereafter, for the defined periods tested monthly from July 1, 2026, through the maturity date, the fixed charge coverage ratio must be not less than <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_ccSbwxZ2eE-Iz8EXGy6S7Q" contextRef="As_Of_7_29_2025_srt_StatementScenarioAxis_xbp_DefinedPeriodsTestedMonthlyFromJuly12026ThroughMaturityDateMember_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_SecondLienSecuredTermLoanMember_kxg4CAHuXU61Rfh8DNpTAA" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xbp:DebtInstrumentCovenantMinimumFixedChargeCoverageRatio" scale="0" id="Narr_PbpsgTWRX06_Y9NA7Cc2Pw">1.00</ix:nonFraction> to 1.00. The Company was in compliance with such financial covenant as of June 30, 2026.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">During the periods August 1, 2025 to December 31, 2025 (Successor) and January 1, 2025 to July 31, 2025 (Predecessor), the Company repaid $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_bmzRMS-W4keOx5FozpRA5w" contextRef="Duration_8_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_SecondLienSecuredTermLoanMember_yHFC4hGlZUW1LPq_9sbnpw" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:RepaymentsOfLongTermDebt" scale="6" id="Narr_0p9wP4G2W0yQQkxQhHhkfg">3.8</ix:nonFraction> million and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_bmzRMS-W4keOx5FozpRA5w" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_7_31_2025_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_SecondLienSecuredTermLoanMember_MEoNsUHBbEOmfgIcKb4Erg" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:RepaymentsOfLongTermDebt" scale="6" id="Narr_1pdjZJJJYEO61Q8NFWsdlw">6.0</ix:nonFraction> million, respectively, in principal amount of the Second Lien Note. During the three and six months ended June 30, 2026 (Successor), the Company repaid $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_bmzRMS-W4keOx5FozpRA5w" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_SecondLienSecuredTermLoanMember_UPbd0Qbvw06EiNmONp1r_g" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:RepaymentsOfLongTermDebt" scale="6" id="Narr_Bou_8ftSZEqqcNCKq2LIig">3.0</ix:nonFraction> million and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_bmzRMS-W4keOx5FozpRA5w" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_SecondLienSecuredTermLoanMember_uZppK6ixWEq35_u356obmA" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:RepaymentsOfLongTermDebt" scale="6" id="Narr_22sz898GwE2l61vitfqIoA">6.3</ix:nonFraction> million principal amount of the Second Lien Note, respectively. The loss on early extinguishment of debt during the three and six months ended June 30, 2026 (Successor) and June 30, 2025 (Predecessor) totaled $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_bmzRMS-W4keOx5FozpRA5w" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_SecondLienSecuredTermLoanMember_uZppK6ixWEq35_u356obmA" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:GainsLossesOnExtinguishmentOfDebt" scale="6" id="Narr_dxVsyGe_CUKEf_RR6Itj0A"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_bmzRMS-W4keOx5FozpRA5w" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2026_To_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_SecondLienSecuredTermLoanMember_UPbd0Qbvw06EiNmONp1r_g" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:GainsLossesOnExtinguishmentOfDebt" scale="6" id="Narr_b4qwwJXD_ESlfcfXSTwDHQ">0</ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction> and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_bmzRMS-W4keOx5FozpRA5w" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_6_30_2025_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_SecondLienSecuredTermLoanMember_wADHDq1UjUyJDBuNs7uqEQ" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:GainsLossesOnExtinguishmentOfDebt" scale="6" id="Narr_UXLCKbob6E-oRnI8YtsIsQ"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_bmzRMS-W4keOx5FozpRA5w" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2025_To_6_30_2025_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_SecondLienSecuredTermLoanMember_3Jh828IZxUWWzMMm0v7SdA" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:GainsLossesOnExtinguishmentOfDebt" scale="6" id="Narr_E1onHhQ7jkamKR9Yci08cw">0.1</ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction> million, respectively, and represents write off of debt issuance costs. Loss on the early extinguishment of debt is reported within debt modification and extinguishment costs (gain), net within the Company&#8217;s condensed consolidated and combined statements of operations. As of June 30, 2026 (Successor), there were borrowings of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_bmzRMS-W4keOx5FozpRA5w" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_SecondLienSecuredTermLoanMember_t_ViUisOX0O7uMeSc9GiGw" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentCarryingAmount" scale="6" id="Narr_-gyCb8Cd2E2xDthfddERow">9.5</ix:nonFraction> million outstanding under the Second Lien Note included in the current portion of long-term debt in the condensed consolidated balance sheets.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">On August 14, 2026, BPA and BRF Finance Co., LLC entered into a Limited Waiver and Fifth Amendment to the Second Lien Note, which, among other things, waived the Specified Events of Default described below under &#8220;ABL Facility.&#8221; See Note 15, <i style="font-style:italic;">Subsequent Events</i>.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">ABL Facility</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">On July 29, 2025, Exela Technologies BPA, LLC and certain of its subsidiaries (collectively, the &#8220;ABL Borrowers&#8221;) entered into a $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_bmzRMS-W4keOx5FozpRA5w" contextRef="As_Of_7_29_2025_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_AblFacilityMaturingJuly292028Member_MgyENkhfKkumt2b0j6AqKQ" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityMaximumBorrowingCapacity" scale="6" id="Narr_0SRqQ5YOnk20pcb8mppkJw">150.0</ix:nonFraction> million Asset-Based Lending Credit and Security Agreement (as amended, the &#8220;ABL Facility&#8221;) with MidCap Funding IV Trust, as administrative and collateral agent (the &#8220;Agent&#8221;), and a syndicate of lenders (the &#8220;ABL Lenders&#8221;). The ABL Facility was executed in connection with BPA&#8217;s emergence from the Chapter 11 Cases and provides for revolving commitments of up to $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_bmzRMS-W4keOx5FozpRA5w" contextRef="As_Of_7_29_2025_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_AblFacilityMaturingJuly292028Member_MgyENkhfKkumt2b0j6AqKQ" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityMaximumBorrowingCapacity" scale="6" id="Narr_mzQn34CrfE-a7LCQCKx_SA">150.0</ix:nonFraction> million, with an option to increase to $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_bmzRMS-W4keOx5FozpRA5w" contextRef="As_Of_7_29_2025_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_AblFacilityMaturingJuly292028Member_MgyENkhfKkumt2b0j6AqKQ" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xbp:LineOfCreditAdditionalBorrowingCapacity" scale="6" id="Narr_4PVwJ81a_ka9_PqDDSaYuQ">175.0</ix:nonFraction> million through an additional tranche. The borrowing availability under the ABL Facility is limited to (a) the lesser of (i) the aggregate revolving commitments and (ii) the borrowing base, which is calculated by reference to eligible billed and unbilled receivables, certain other receivables, eligible cash, and related assets, reduced by reserves established by the Agent, minus (b) the availability block (described below). Borrowings under the ABL Facility bear an interest at Term <span style="-sec-ix-hidden:Hidden_7qRvnVbCKUGBzVe6kzDXbg;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">SOFR</span></span> plus an applicable margin ranging from <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_ccSbwxZ2eE-Iz8EXGy6S7Q" contextRef="Duration_7_29_2025_To_7_29_2025_srt_RangeAxis_srt_MinimumMember_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_AblFacilityMaturingJuly292028Member_edi3UZVUGE2JM5gwA4t16A" decimals="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentBasisSpreadOnVariableRate1" scale="-2" id="Narr_4Mrls5ZjTE6YuMm0ARnWLg">3.8</ix:nonFraction>% to <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_ccSbwxZ2eE-Iz8EXGy6S7Q" contextRef="Duration_7_29_2025_To_7_29_2025_srt_RangeAxis_srt_MaximumMember_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_AblFacilityMaturingJuly292028Member_alqEkwxfzEqj8mNGRp2Z3A" decimals="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentBasisSpreadOnVariableRate1" scale="-2" id="Narr_H4_synedMUGfG3m_Lcxm-Q">4.3</ix:nonFraction>%, depending on the ABL Borrowers&#8217; trailing twelve-month EBITDA, subject to a <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_ccSbwxZ2eE-Iz8EXGy6S7Q" contextRef="As_Of_7_29_2025_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_AblFacilityMaturingJuly292028Member_MgyENkhfKkumt2b0j6AqKQ" decimals="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xbp:DebtInstrumentFloorRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_-Z4bN5FGUE6sP8hkouXtMA">1.0</ix:nonFraction>% SOFR floor. Interest is payable monthly, with a <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_ccSbwxZ2eE-Iz8EXGy6S7Q" contextRef="Duration_7_29_2025_To_7_29_2025_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_AblFacilityMaturingJuly292028Member_mo3dEm3OP0aAXP1O5UUfWw" decimals="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xbp:DebtInstrumentDefaultPremiumPercentage" scale="-2" id="Narr_puCAy_XEu0SdDaAngui99g">2.0</ix:nonFraction>% default premium. In addition to interest, the ABL Borrowers are required to pay an unused commitment fee of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_ccSbwxZ2eE-Iz8EXGy6S7Q" contextRef="Duration_7_29_2025_To_7_29_2025_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_AblFacilityMaturingJuly292028Member_mo3dEm3OP0aAXP1O5UUfWw" decimals="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityUnusedCapacityCommitmentFeePercentage" scale="-2" id="Narr_BcfojWQMvkKN064i_fbmzA">0.5</ix:nonFraction>% per annum on the average daily unused portion of the commitments, customary letter of credit fees on the face amount of each outstanding letter of credit, a collateral management fee payable to the Agent, and a minimum balance fee if borrowings under the ABL Facility fall below <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_ccSbwxZ2eE-Iz8EXGy6S7Q" contextRef="Duration_7_29_2025_To_7_29_2025_srt_RangeAxis_srt_MinimumMember_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_AblFacilityMaturingJuly292028Member_edi3UZVUGE2JM5gwA4t16A" decimals="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xbp:LineOfCreditFacilityThresholdBorrowingsBaseTriggerPercentageForPaymentOfMinimumBalanceFee" scale="-2" id="Narr_AEJ13axZU0-WzYig9PwnAg">20.0</ix:nonFraction>% of the Borrowing Base. </p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">As of June 30, 2026 (Successor), there were borrowings of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_bmzRMS-W4keOx5FozpRA5w" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_AblFacilityMaturingJuly292028Member_gTlu7trxwkqA1piGUSSqnQ" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentCarryingAmount" scale="6" id="Narr_01JoFWGwf0yDoTJjO0KlMQ">63.3</ix:nonFraction> million outstanding under the ABL Facility. There were unamortized debt issuance costs of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_bmzRMS-W4keOx5FozpRA5w" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_AblFacilityMaturingJuly292028Member_gTlu7trxwkqA1piGUSSqnQ" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DeferredFinanceCostsNoncurrentNet" scale="6" id="Narr_s9Ajv0u-jUq2RsW216hR4Q">1.7</ix:nonFraction> million on the ABL Facility as of June 30, 2026 included in other noncurrent assets on the condensed consolidated balance sheet. The ABL Facility matures on July 29, 2028, and may be prepaid at any time without penalty (other than breakage costs). Mandatory repayments are required from proceeds of dispositions of the ABL Priority Collateral, certain insurance proceeds, or upon acceleration following an event of default. The events of default include failure to pay principal, interest or fees when due; breaches of covenants or other material contractual obligations; materially inaccurate representations or warranties; failure to pay specified other indebtedness above $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_bmzRMS-W4keOx5FozpRA5w" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_AblFacilityMaturingJuly292028Member_gTlu7trxwkqA1piGUSSqnQ" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xbp:DebtInstrumentDebtDefaultMinimumThresholdAmount" scale="6" id="Narr_H-el1DtQ0EKfFNQhyyjUTQ">25.0</ix:nonFraction> million; bankruptcy or insolvency; final unsatisfied judgments; ERISA-related defaults; and a change in control.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt;">The obligations under the ABL Facility are guaranteed on a joint and several basis by substantially all of the ABL Borrowers&#8217; U.S. subsidiaries. The liens securing the ABL Facility are subject to an Intercreditor Agreement (the &#8220;ABL Intercreditor Agreement&#8221;) dated July 29, 2025, among MidCap Funding IV Trust, Ankura Trust Company, LLC, </p></ix:continuation></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">27</p></div></div>
<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:79.3%;border:0;margin:30pt 10.35% 30pt 10.35%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:10.35%;padding-right:10.35%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:21.6pt;min-height:41.75pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;margin:0pt 0pt 30pt 0pt;"><a href="#TOC"><span style="font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Table of Contents</span></a></p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><ix:continuation id="Tb_dxRbl05eoEqfraXHXS3sTg_cont4" continuedAt="Tb_dxRbl05eoEqfraXHXS3sTg_cont5"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">as Term Agent, BRF Finance Co., LLC, as Riley Agent, and U.S. Bank Trust Company, National Association, as July 2030 Notes Trustee. The ABL Intercreditor Agreement governs lien priorities including (i) relative priorities for the collateral securing the ABL Facility obligations, the Super Senior Term Loan obligations, the July 2030 Notes Indenture obligations and the Second Lien Note obligations; (ii) collateral priorities securing (a) any Second Lien Note obligations, (b) any Super Senior Term Loan obligations, (c) any July 2030 Notes Indenture obligations, or (d) any Excess ABL Debt; and (iii) prohibition on contesting liens. The ABL Facility is secured by a first-priority lien on certain ABL Priority Collateral (including receivables, cash, inventory, deposit accounts, and related assets) and a junior lien on certain Term Priority Collateral (as defined therein), subject to the ABL Intercreditor Agreement. On May 14, 2026, the ABL Borrowers, the Agent and the ABL Lenders entered into an amendment to the ABL Facility to permit ongoing sales of designated receivables under the Amended BR Exar AR Facility, subject to a cap of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_bmzRMS-W4keOx5FozpRA5w" contextRef="As_Of_5_14_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_AblFacilityMaturingJuly292028Member_Nn5-4F5pLkmsVASuXZTaSg" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xbp:MaximumPermittedSalesOfDesignatedReceivables" scale="6" id="Narr_MVuBnkhDE0uRXFMLZZV0Eg">10.0</ix:nonFraction> million in the aggregate amounts outstanding. </p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The ABL Facility includes customary affirmative covenants such as reporting, collateral maintenance, insurance, and inspections, and negative covenants, including restrictions on additional indebtedness, liens, asset sales, investments, affiliate transactions, and changes in business. The ABL Facility also includes a financial covenant requiring the ABL Borrowers to maintain a minimum fixed charge coverage ratio, calculated on a trailing twelve-month basis. The fixed charge coverage ratio is defined as the ratio of EBITDA less Unfinanced Capital Expenditures less Capitalized Software Expenditures, to Fixed Charges (as such terms are defined in the ABL Facility). The minimum required ratio varies depending on the period: for the defined periods tested quarterly through December 31, 2025, and monthly from January 1, 2026 through June 30, 2026, the fixed charge coverage ratio must be not less than <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_ccSbwxZ2eE-Iz8EXGy6S7Q" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_srt_StatementScenarioAxis_xbp_DefinedPeriodTestedQuarterlyThroughDecember312025AndMonthlyFromJanuary12026ThroughJune302026Member_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_AblFacilityMaturingJuly292028Member_Qt0LJnSexUeaoq56B0s_lA" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xbp:DebtInstrumentCovenantMinimumFixedChargeCoverageRatio" scale="0" id="Narr_-qLpG-n3Gk2yl1M8LkBqTA">0.85</ix:nonFraction> to 1.00. Thereafter, for the defined periods tested monthly from July 1, 2026, through the maturity date, the fixed charge coverage ratio must be not less than <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_ccSbwxZ2eE-Iz8EXGy6S7Q" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_srt_StatementScenarioAxis_xbp_DefinedPeriodsTestedMonthlyFromJuly12026ThroughMaturityDateMember_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_AblFacilityMaturingJuly292028Member_WM1oXDAwmEOqCLkeMQEBqw" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xbp:DebtInstrumentCovenantMinimumFixedChargeCoverageRatio" scale="0" id="Narr_yMGn-t6smUmoYQhQQo9sVw">1.00</ix:nonFraction> to 1.00. On March 6, 2026, the ABL Borrowers, the Agent and the ABL Lenders entered into a Limited Waiver and Third Amendment to the ABL Facility. Among other things, this amendment (i) eliminates a covenant requiring the ABL Borrower to maintain a minimum excess availability of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_bmzRMS-W4keOx5FozpRA5w" contextRef="As_Of_3_6_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_AblFacilityMaturingJuly292028Member_Rl2PrEnrd0uzdjHKWBsBog" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xbp:DebtInstrumentCovenantMinimumLiquidityRequirement" scale="6" id="Narr_C9j8u0T4gEmeYBCbzhcfoA">7.5</ix:nonFraction> million; (ii) implements a temporary availability block through June 30, 2026, which reduces borrowing capacity by the greater of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_bmzRMS-W4keOx5FozpRA5w" contextRef="As_Of_3_6_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_AblFacilityMaturingJuly292028Member_Rl2PrEnrd0uzdjHKWBsBog" decimals="-4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xbp:DebtInstrumentReducedBorrowingCapacity" scale="6" id="Narr_-zw93RkvKkGvZVqdFZ37qA">3.75</ix:nonFraction> million or <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_ccSbwxZ2eE-Iz8EXGy6S7Q" contextRef="As_Of_3_6_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_AblFacilityMaturingJuly292028Member_Rl2PrEnrd0uzdjHKWBsBog" decimals="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xbp:DebtInstrumentPercentageOfBorrowingCapacityBy" scale="-2" id="Narr__aPNslmrY0S5NRtY0Pl1zQ">5.0</ix:nonFraction>% of the borrowing base if the ABL Borrower&#8217;s fixed charge coverage ratio falls below <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_ccSbwxZ2eE-Iz8EXGy6S7Q" contextRef="As_Of_3_6_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_AblFacilityMaturingJuly292028Member_Rl2PrEnrd0uzdjHKWBsBog" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xbp:DebtInstrumentCovenantMinimumFixedChargeCoverageRatio" scale="0" id="Narr_Q3Rb5eYGCUW9akKqKxNcdQ">1.00</ix:nonFraction> to 1.00; (iii) temporarily increases the advance rate for eligible investment grade billed accounts to <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_ccSbwxZ2eE-Iz8EXGy6S7Q" contextRef="As_Of_3_6_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_AblFacilityMaturingJuly292028Member_Rl2PrEnrd0uzdjHKWBsBog" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xbp:DebtInstrumentAdvanceRateForEligibleInvestmentGradeBilledAccounts" scale="-2" id="Narr_4Rx20K9yD06PNT4ws1N3Ew">95.0</ix:nonFraction>% through September 30, 2026; (iv) adjusts the calculation of the borrowing base; (v) amends the mechanics governing the cash dominion period; and (vi) resets the deferred revolving loan origination fee. The Company was in compliance with such financial covenants as of June 30, 2026.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The Company did not make certain tax payments required to be made under the Plan, including payments due on or before July 29, 2026 to holders of Priority Tax Claims, and did not provide notice of the resulting defaults within the three-day period required under the ABL Facility (collectively, the &#8220;Specified Events of Default&#8221;). Specified Events of Default constituted events of default under the ABL Facility and gave rise to cross-defaults under the Company&#8217;s other financing agreements. On August 14, 2026, the ABL Borrowers, the Agent and the ABL Lenders entered into a Limited Waiver and Sixth Amendment to the ABL Facility, which waived the Specified Events of Default and, among other things, adjusted the calculation of the borrowing base to exclude certain receivables. See Note 15, <i style="font-style:italic;">Subsequent Events</i>.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">European Senior Credit Facilities Agreement</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;line-height:1.19;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt;">In June 2024, XBP Europe, Inc., a wholly owned subsidiary of the Company, together with certain other subsidiaries, entered into a Facilities Agreement (the &#8220;Facilities Agreement&#8221;) with HSBC UK Bank plc (&#8220;HSBC&#8221;) for a &#163;<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_GBP_BosIxpI2_0iK7Ehy-DTuLw" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2024_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_FacilitiesAgreement2024Member_hjU4uGrdYECM7s2tdT7tBw" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityMaximumBorrowingCapacity" scale="6" id="Narr_gI82n36GhkuR_yIAHpjWCg">15.0</ix:nonFraction> million and &#8364;<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_EUR_Np8_fFq8_kObu1zLYIauwg" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2024_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_FacilitiesAgreement2024Member_hjU4uGrdYECM7s2tdT7tBw" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityMaximumBorrowingCapacity" scale="6" id="Narr_0ADfQV1Dwk6KzQmXzLb1sg">10.5</ix:nonFraction> million secured credit facility consisting of (i) a single draw, secured Term Loan A facility in an aggregate principal amount of &#163;<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_GBP_BosIxpI2_0iK7Ehy-DTuLw" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2024_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_TermLoan2028FacilityMember_L3ZjoFRCCEiiwnfaxPq6lQ" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityMaximumBorrowingCapacity" scale="6" id="Narr_zkvM04Pze0GZdxzOkqTUUg">3.0</ix:nonFraction> million (the &#8220;2028 Term Loan A Facility&#8221;), (ii) a single draw, secured Term Loan B facility in an aggregate principal amount of &#8364;<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_EUR_Np8_fFq8_kObu1zLYIauwg" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2024_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_TermLoan2028BFacilityMember_qaNjrInxzUGYGgmkQBy9_w" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityMaximumBorrowingCapacity" scale="6" id="Narr_eyWSxFGhwEquQhqPN95K2g">10.5</ix:nonFraction> million (the &#8220;2028 Term Loan B Facility&#8221;, collectively with the 2028 Term Loan A Facility, the &#8220;2028 Term Loan Facilities&#8221;) and (iii) a multi-draw, multi-currency secured revolving credit facility in an aggregate principal amount of &#163;<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_GBP_BosIxpI2_0iK7Ehy-DTuLw" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2024_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_us-gaap_RevolvingCreditFacilityMember_8u7oY31OrkGYMPs-hiqCQQ" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityMaximumBorrowingCapacity" scale="6" id="Narr_M9HKuaThTUSQ8KYtuqT9Xg">12.0</ix:nonFraction> million (the &#8220;Revolving Credit Facility&#8221;), and, together with the 2028 Term Loan Facilities, (the &#8220;European Senior Credit Facilities&#8221;). Pursuant to the original Facilities Agreement, the 2028 Term Loan Facilities mature on June 26, 2028, and the Revolving Credit Facility matures on June 26, 2027, with certain extension rights at the discretion of HSBC. Borrowings under the 2028 Term Loan A Facility, the 2028 Term Loan B Facility and Revolving Credit Facility bear interest at a rate per annum equal to the SONIA plus the applicable margin of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_ccSbwxZ2eE-Iz8EXGy6S7Q" contextRef="Duration_6_1_2024_To_6_30_2024_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_TermLoan2028FacilityMember_us-gaap_VariableRateAxis_xbp_SterlingOvernightIndexAverageMember_0Pk_o3hB7024c6N9rqlHXw" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentBasisSpreadOnVariableRate1" scale="-2" id="Narr_x-Rk_F7Uv0u4uZcIgTYI1w">3.25</ix:nonFracti